at least 12 people were killed overnight  in a plane crash in the Central Asian  country of Kazakhstan the aircraft  slammed into a two-story building  shortly after takeoff 93 passengers and  five crew members were on board dozens  of them were hurt the flight was  traveling from Almaty Kazakhstan largest  city to the country's capital Roxana  Saberi is following the story Roxana  what more can you tell us good morning  the plane ran into trouble shortly after  taking off from southeastern Kazakhstan  the survivor told local media the jet  that started falling and people were  screaming and crying images show the  front of the Beck airplane smashed into  a building in a residential area just  outside the airport with the rear of the  plane laying in a field nearby and video  posted online shows rescuers digging  through rubble searching for survivors  and a small child being carried away  from the scene the country's deputy  prime minister said the runway was in  ideal condition authorities are  investigating whether the crash was  caused by pilot error or technical  problems the state news agency says both  flight data recorders have been found in  good shape which should assist with a  quick analysis of the cause of the crash  in the meantime authorities have  suspended all flights in the budget  airline and the Dutch made Fokker 100  production of the aircraft ended more  than two decades ago but around 140 of  them are still active mainly in  Australia and Iran Vlad I'll take it  Roxana thank you Roxana Saberi force in  London  you
 

